he mural was painted by two asylum seekers from that oppressive…"],["Toulouse-Lautrec","sight",38.92142,-77.04193,"2433 18th St NW","","","","","r","Contrary to popular belief, this huge two-story mural is not of the famous French painter, it is a mural reproduction of one of his paintings. The man in question is Aristide Bruant, a then-popular French cabaret performer."],["Walter Pierce Park Mural","sight",38.92405,-77.04542,"","","","","","r","This is a sadder mural, a memorial by Aniekan Udofia to two teenagers who were murdered near this park."],["District of Columbia Arts Center","activity",38.92164,-77.04257,"2438 18th St NW","Gallery: Wed-Sun 2PM-7PM","","","","r","The Arts Center has an art gallery with rotating high-quality shows by local artists, as well as a very cool black box theater, and regular and special events (like avant garde poetry nights)."],["National Zoo","sight",38.93108,-77.04973,"3001 Connecticut Ave NW","8AM-7PM; winter: 8AM-5PM, last admission 1 hour before closing","","","","r","A collection of 400 species, including 2,000 animals. Get a map at the entrance, take your time, and be prepared to walk a great deal. Bring water—the concessions here are insultingly expensive. The most crowded exhibits are nearly…"],["Peirce Mill","sight",38.94,-77.05222,"2401 Tilden St NW","Milling Demonstrations: April-October on 2nd and 4th Sat, 11AM-2PM","","","","r","A historic water-powered mill in the park and a national historic site built by Isaac Peirce in 1829."],["Vace's Pizza","restaurant",38.93401,-77.05716,"3315 Connecticut Ave NW","Mon-Fri 9AM-9PM, Sat 9AM-8PM, Sun 10AM-5PM","","","","r","Another contender for D.C.'s best pizza is this hole in the wall Italian deli. The pizza is 100% authentic New York-style, cheap and done well (the subs are great too). No tables or delivery—carry out only. Whole pizza or by the slice.…"]]}